c31a293bac59616e8fe041e65cdd9b380967d3865ac6a1f2a547a11"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:project.symbol-reference-completeness","usage":{"input_tokens":42244,"output_tokens":2106,"requests":3}}],"version":1},"findings":[{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify the ContextVar RETIRE discipline: material_child_index() must use the set/reset-token pattern so only the outermost (creating) activation resets/clears the index on exit, and a nested inner exit is a no-op that leaves the outer's snapshot intact.","cohort":["E3","E5","F4","G5","T6","T9","necessity","project.engine-layer-enforcement","project.portability"],"criteria":["T9"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.1722,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Approach: 'derive_plan_material_pin_health (attest.py:54) opens the context around its derive_health call ... and plan_review_health (src/rebar/audit/read.py:58) opens it around the verify+compute_validity pair' — establishes nesting","Approach: 'Activation is idempotent (an outer context wins)' names create-time idempotency but not exit/reset behavior","Approach: 'No caching survives the call' asserts retirement but does not specify the ContextVar reset token pattern that makes inner-exit a no-op when nested"],"finding":"The ContextVar-scoped child-index snapshot's RETIRE/reset semantics under nesting are unspecified: both plan_review_health (read.py:58, outer) and derive_plan_material_pin_health (attest.py:54, inner) open material_child_index(), so contexts nest. The plan states activation is idempotent ('an outer context wins') but does not state that exiting the INNER context must NOT reset/clear the index while the OUTER context is still active. Without a token-restore (set/reset) discipline, the inner __exit__ could tear down the shared snapshot mid-derivation, silently reverting live_material_children to the O(pins) slow path — or worse leave a stale index bound.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f079cd8aace206e28","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach — 'Activation is idempotent (an outer context wins)'; Scope entries for relation_snapshot.py, attest.py, read.py","norm_id":"n4c4acc368f17da4f","priority":0.7778,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["read.py opens the outer context, calls into derive_plan_material_pin_health which opens the inner context; when the inner context exits (per-pin derivation done), if it unconditionally resets the ContextVar the outer compute_validity path loses the index and rescans the full store — reintroducing the exact O(pins) stall the plan set out to fix","A future caller that opens material_child_index() around a loop of derivations relies on the reset being scoped only to its own token, not the innermost activation"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"State that material_child_index() captures the ContextVar Token on set and, in a finally, only resets it when the current activation was the creator (outer wins on both create and retire); add a scan-count assertion on the plan_review_health (read.py) path — not just compute_validity — to prove the outer snapshot survives the inner derivation's context exit.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.7778,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Re-anchor AC3 on the deterministic in-session metric (scan count ≤2 per plan_review_health derivation, asserted by the new test / instrumented single-run count) and demote the concurrent-load wall-time comparison to informational context, so the criterion is provable without reproducing the 20-session load window.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e"],"criteria":["F1"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.525,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'completes in the same order of magnitude as one rebar list --parent ... (checked by re-running the RCA's instrumented timing: scan count drops from 89 to ≤2, wall time from ~745 s to within ~10x of the single-scan list time in the same load window)'","Reproducing '20 concurrent rebar CLI processes' + a 5247-ticket store is an environment condition unlikely to be reproducible on demand in-session."],"finding":"AC3's wall-time proof ('within ~10x of the single-scan list time in the same load window') depends on reproducing a ~20-concurrent-session real-store load environment, which is not deterministically evaluable in one working session; the durable in-session proof is the deterministic scan-count drop (89→≤2), while the wall-time-under-load portion is environment-dependent.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f96913c2f75812e92","impact":0.44,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria, AC3","norm_id":"nc189cf2967c600eb","priority":0.275,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Reviewer/agent tries to close AC3 but cannot reconstitute the original concurrent load window, leaving the criterion effectively unverifiable."],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split AC3: (a) deterministic — instrumented single-process run of plan_review_health on 2ddd-... shows reduce_all_tickets scan count ≤2 (was 89); (b) informational — wall-time-under-load comparison recorded if the load window can be reproduced, else noted as observed-once in the RCA.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.625,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Capture the material_child_index activation contract (who opens it, idempotent outer-wins nesting, that live_material_children must be reached only within an active context to get the fast path) in a short module docstring on relation_snapshot.py or an AGENTS.md/ADR note.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e"],"criteria":["T5e"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.7437,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'Add a ContextVar-scoped child-index snapshot ... a context manager (material_child_index()) ... Activation is idempotent (an outer context wins).'","Three modules coordinate via an implicit ContextVar; no doc/ADR entry is listed in Scope to record the activation-boundary and outer-wins nesting invariant."],"finding":"The plan introduces a novel cross-module contract — a ContextVar-scoped, idempotent (outer-wins) child-index snapshot activated in attest.py and audit/read.py and consumed by relation_snapshot.py — but does not capture this activation/nesting protocol in any ADR, AGENTS.md, or module docstring, so a future editor adding a third call site could nest incorrectly or bypass the snapshot.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f74ee00602f4a1889","impact":0.33,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach / Scope (relation_snapshot.py material_child_index, attest.py, audit/read.py)","norm_id":"n3dd360b7e7f6a899","priority":0.2063,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A later change adds a new plan_review_health caller and forgets to open the context, silently regressing to O(pins) scans without any test catching it."],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.625,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}}],"impact_model_version":"plan-v5","material_fingerprint":"bc809c443472ed77","material_parts":{"children":["647ea2107ca5072f",0],"description":["43887785cfca2cf2",5957],"descri